<title>UK: UK approves Firststeel buyout by Brit Steel.</title>
<headline>UK approves Firststeel buyout by Brit Steel.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain on Friday said it would not refer the acquisition of Firststeel Holdings Ltd by British Steel to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission.</p>
<p>The secretary of state for trade and industry, Ian Lang, said the government had also approved the acquistiion of Alpha Beta Ltd by BTP Chemicals and the takeover of Westbury Hotels by Chelsfield Plc.</p>
<p>The acquisitions of Harrisons &amp; Sons Ltd by De La Rue Plc and of Radio Wyvern Plc by GWR Group Plc were also approved and would not be referred to the commission.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
